How can cities effectively reduce traffi:
Cities can reduce traffic congestion while maintaining accessibility through several strategies. Improving public transportation systems is crucial; enhancing the coverage, frequency, and reliability of buses, trains, and trams can encourage more people to use these options instead of personal vehicles. Additionally, developing dedicated bike lanes and pedestrian pathways promotes active transportation and encourages people to walk or cycle.

Implementing congestion pricing can also help manage demand by charging drivers to enter high-traffic areas during peak times, thereby incentivizing the use of alternative transportation methods. Cities can improve traffic signal management with smart technology to optimize traffic flow and reduce waiting times.

